Backport of the Go 1.27 json/v2 changes trivy needs, from upstream
aquasecurity/trivy dc3c56eed5 "chore: bump Go to 1.27 (#11127)" (2026-08-21,
on main; not in any release as of v0.74.0). Drop at the next trivy release.

Go 1.27's encoding/json/v2 changed two things trivy v0.74.0 relies on:
- `json.SkipFunc` is gone; the "fall back to default decoding" sentinel is
  now `errors.ErrUnsupported`. Two call sites (both COMPILE errors on 1.27.1):
  pkg/x/json/json.go and pkg/iac/scanners/cloudformation/parser/parameter.go.
- the struct-tag option `inline` became `embed`. pkg/result/filter.go still
  COMPILES with the old tag but would silently change the shape of trivy's
  JSON output, so it is taken too.
Verified against the full v0.74.0 source: these are the only SkipFunc uses and
the only `,inline` JSON tag. The rest of that upstream commit (errors.AsType,
reflect.TypeAssert, strings.Cut) is style-only on Go 1.27 and is not needed.

diff --git a/pkg/x/json/json.go b/pkg/x/json/json.go
--- a/pkg/x/json/json.go
+++ b/pkg/x/json/json.go
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@ import (
 	"bytes"
 	"encoding/json/jsontext"
 	"encoding/json/v2"
+	"errors"
 	"io"
 
 	"golang.org/x/xerrors"
@@ -106,7 +107,8 @@ func unmarshaler[T any](r *lineReader, visited set.Set[int], hooks ...DecodeHook
 
 		// Check visited set to avoid infinity loops
 		if visited.Contains(start) {
-			return json.SkipFunc
+			// Fall back to the default decoding.
+			return errors.ErrUnsupported
 		}
 		visited.Append(start)
 
diff --git a/pkg/iac/scanners/cloudformation/parser/parameter.go b/pkg/iac/scanners/cloudformation/parser/parameter.go
--- a/pkg/iac/scanners/cloudformation/parser/parameter.go
+++ b/pkg/iac/scanners/cloudformation/parser/parameter.go
@@ -54,7 +54,8 @@ func unmarshalIntFirst(dec *jsontext.Decoder, v *any) error {
 		}
 		return nil
 	}
-	return json.SkipFunc
+	// Fall back to the default decoding.
+	return errors.ErrUnsupported
 }
 
 func (p *Parameter) Type() cftypes.CfType {
diff --git a/pkg/result/filter.go b/pkg/result/filter.go
--- a/pkg/result/filter.go
